  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Unsettled weather will persist through next week\nwith daily thunderstorm chances.\n\nA rather stagnant pattern will remain in place with daily\nchances of afternoon/evening thunderstorms. A large ridge over \nthe Atlantic with a subtle trough across the Great Lakes \ncontinues to supply persistent southerly flow, advecting a warm \nand moist airmass into the region. Forcing will remain weak, so\ndaily storms will mainly develop as a result of differential \nheating and terrain. Precipitable Water values continue to be in\nexcess of 1.50\" so rainfall will be very efficient in storms, \nand localized flooding could occur if any storm persist over the\nsame area for any length of time. \n\nBy tomorrow, ridging over the Atlantic will begin to shift \nsouth and weaken as a broad upper trough begins to push south \nover the Mid Atlantic. With slightly better upper support \nleading to better forcing in addition to modest shear and \nmoderate/strong instability, a more organized storm threat may \nbe possible Tue-Thu. Along with any severe threat, a flash \nflooding threat will persist into next week as well.",
